  "summary": "John Preskill frames the NISQ era as a real scientific threshold but warns against overclaiming near-term commercial transformation. Devices around 50 to a few hundred noisy qubits may illuminate many-body quantum physics and test heuristic algorithms, yet gate errors, circuit-depth limits, and error-correction overhead keep transformative fault-tolerant applications at a longer horizon.",
